# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify rewrites.
# Serve the Mobile Repair page at a real address, stardockmarine.com/repair,
# without a redirect (status 200 = rewrite, the URL stays /repair). The page
# itself is index.html; its <link rel="canonical"> names /repair as the one
# URL search engines should index for the repair content. /repair/ (with a
# slash) redirects to /repair so the page's relative image/script paths resolve.
/repair   /index.html   200
/repair/  /repair        301

# Old / stray addresses. Without a 404.html the host served index.html at ANY
# path (so /boat-repair/outboard showed the page with broken CSS and images,
# because its relative asset links resolved under /boat-repair/). Send the
# known old paths to /repair; everything else now gets the real 404 page.
/boat-repair/*   /repair   301
/boat-repair     /repair   301
